turnip: darwin, the device's GPU window is its own connection's, not the enumeration probe's

tu_knl_darwin_load opens a connection for the facts (Query, GetDeviceInfo: its slot's GPU window va_start/va_size), stores them in the
physical device and closes it; darwin_device_init opens the device's own connection. That one can land in another slot (the probe's
slot still going away, or another process opening in between), with another window, while the VA heap was still seeded from the
probe's: every BoMap then fell outside the window the kernel checks and was refused with BadArgument (the first macOS desktop on
piano, run attend4: "Installer Progress[102] slot 5 BoMap -> BadArgument", "MenuBarAgent[203] slot 5 BoMap -> BadArgument", both
processes' Metal devices dead). Now the device takes the window GetDeviceInfo gave its own connection before the heap is seeded, and
says so once on stderr when it differs: "NativeAdreno: this device's GPU window is 0x... + 0x..., the enumeration probe's was ...".
Against the tree after 0001-0005. MIT, as the file.

--- a/src/freedreno/vulkan/tu_knl_darwin.cc
+++ b/src/freedreno/vulkan/tu_knl_darwin.cc
@@ -1623,6 +1623,20 @@
       if (result != VK_SUCCESS)
          return result;
    }
+   /* This connection may sit in another slot than the probe's, with another GPU window (the probe's slot still going away, another
+    * process opening in between): the kernel refuses every BoMap outside the window GetDeviceInfo just gave this connection
+    * (BadArgument), so the device's addresses come from that window, not the probe's. The VA heap is seeded at the first allocation. */
+   if (!dw.virtgpu && dw.info.va_size &&
+       (dw.info.va_start != dev->physical_device->va_start || dw.info.va_size != dev->physical_device->va_size)) {
+      mesa_loge("NativeAdreno: this device's GPU window is %#llx + %#llx, the enumeration probe's was %#llx + %#llx (another slot); "
+                "the device takes its own", (unsigned long long)dw.info.va_start, (unsigned long long)dw.info.va_size,
+                (unsigned long long)dev->physical_device->va_start, (unsigned long long)dev->physical_device->va_size);
+      dev->physical_device->va_start = dw.info.va_start;
+      dev->physical_device->va_size = dw.info.va_size;
+   }
+   /* tu_CreateDevice copied the probe's window into the device before this call (its own VMA heap is made after it, from these). */
+   dev->va_start = dev->physical_device->va_start;
+   dev->va_size = dev->physical_device->va_size;
    struct darwin_retire_state *retire = (struct darwin_retire_state *)
       vk_zalloc(&dev->vk.alloc, sizeof(*retire), 8, VK_SYSTEM_ALLOCATION_SCOPE_DEVICE);
    if (!retire) {
